# 05 - CR14 Design: After-Hours Contractor Access

## Requirement

Limited wireless access for cleaning and security contractors, after hours only.

## Design decision

Milestone 1 proposed a time-based ACL. The Packet Tracer IOS used does not reliably support `time-range`, `periodic` or `kron`, so the design uses two pre-staged states switched by a documented procedure. VLAN 70 keeps its own subnet (10.34.70.0/24), SSID (Contractor-CR14) and ACL treatment.

| State | Router0: inbound ACL on Gi0/0.70 | Switch0 Fa0/6 (AP-Contractor) | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| BUSINESS-HOURS (default, saved in startup-config) | CR14-BUSINESS-HOURS (deny all) | shutdown | Contractor Wi-Fi unavailable |
| AFTER-HOURS | CR14-AFTER-HOURS (limited internet) | no shutdown | DNS, web and ping to the internet only; no internal access |

Two independent controls (ACL and AP port) are used together, and the default state is fail-closed.

## ACLs

```
ip access-list extended CR14-AFTER-HOURS
 permit udp any host 255.255.255.255 eq 67
 permit udp any host 10.34.50.10 eq 67
 deny ip any 10.34.0.0 0.0.255.255
 deny ip any 203.0.113.0 0.0.0.3
 permit udp any any eq 53
 permit tcp any any eq 80
 permit tcp any any eq 443
 permit icmp any any echo
 deny ip any any

ip access-list extended CR14-BUSINESS-HOURS
 deny ip any any
```

## Switching between states

`config/cr14-after-hours.txt`

```
! Router0
configure terminal
interface g0/0.70
 ip access-group CR14-AFTER-HOURS in
end
! Switch0
configure terminal
interface f0/6
 no shutdown
end
```

`config/cr14-business-hours.txt`

```
! Router0
configure terminal
interface g0/0.70
 ip access-group CR14-BUSINESS-HOURS in
end
! Switch0
configure terminal
interface f0/6
 shutdown
end
```

Verify with `show ip interface g0/0.70` (inbound access list) and `show ip access-lists` (match counters).

## Limitation

Enforcement of the schedule is procedural: an administrator must run the scripts at the start and end of the after-hours period. On production IOS the same ACL names could be driven by `time-range` or `kron` without changing the rest of the design.
